-- title:
--   The first four Frobenius degree sums are $5,5,20,89$
-- statement:
--   Let $N_d$ be the number of degree-$d$ places of the level-$25$ function field over $𝔽_3$. For each $m\in\{1,2,3,4\}$, the weighted divisor sum is $$\sum_{d\mid m}dN_d=(5,5,20,89)_m.$$ This converts the four extension-field point counts into the first four closed-place moments used in the zeta calculation. Formalization note: the theorem indexes $m=1,2,3,4$ by an element of a four-element finite type.
-- source:
--   B. Mazur, Modular curves and the Eisenstein ideal, Publ. IHES 47 (1977); Lean formalization of the order-25 case for this mission. Modules in the MazurProof/Keystone/Tate families are adapted from anthropics/fermats-last-theorem (Apache-2.0) via the xiangyazi24/FLT fork.

